  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "f7bfda95",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Week 2 – ML Task Framing\n",
    "\n",
    "## My Lane\n",
    "**Lane:** Decline Recovery"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ce51746a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. My Lane as an ML Task\n",
    "\n",
    "**Task Type:** Ranking\n",
    "\n",
    "The goal is to rank content pages by review priority so the SEO/content team knows which pages should be reviewed first for possible performance decline."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "627022b8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Target (or Proxy)\n",
    "\n",
    "The ideal target is whether a page needs review. Since that label is unavailable, a proxy label is used:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `is_declining_label` derived from `trend_direction == \"down\"`.\n",
    "\n",
    "This proxy represents whether a page is currently declining."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "588433b2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Success Metric\n",
    "\n",
    "**Precision@K** is used because only the top-ranked pages will be reviewed. It measures what fraction of the top K recommended pages are actually declining."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7fb2ae7e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(\"data/raw/content_refresh_anonymized.csv\")\n",
    "df[\"is_declining_label\"] = (df[\"trend_direction\"].str.lower()==\"down\").astype(int)\n",
    "df.head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "59f01309",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Unit of Analysis\n",
    "\n",
    "**One row = one content page.**\n",
    "\n",
    "Each row contains signals such as impressions, CTR, average position, content age, and days since last update."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7b95e1e8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "print(df.shape)\n",
    "df[[\"impressions_90d\",\"ctr\",\"avg_position\",\"days_since_last_update\",\"content_age_days\",\"is_declining_label\"]].head()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "93a2abcf",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 5. Why ML Beats a Fixed Rule\n",
    "\n",
    "A simple rule such as \"review every page older than 180 days\" ignores other useful signals like impressions, CTR, ranking position, and content age. Machine learning combines multiple features and learns patterns that provide a better ranking of pages than a single manually written rule."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3122d80c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 6. Real Business Action\n",
    "\n",
    "The ranked output helps the content team:\n",
    "- Prioritize which pages to review first.\n",
    "- Spend editing time on pages with the highest risk of decline.\n",
    "- Improve search performance more efficiently."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0a30d47d",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 7. Self-Check\n",
    "\n",
